From: Altium-on-Wine kit
Subject: winemac: preserve the stacking order of retired client views

Rapid switches can leave multiple Metal canvases awaiting a replacement
frame. Putting each retired view at the bottom leaves the oldest canvas
above all the newer fallbacks. Put each fallback above the one retired
before it and keep live views above that stack.

--- a/dlls/winemac.drv/cocoa_window.m
+++ b/dlls/winemac.drv/cocoa_window.m
@@ -634,10 +634,16 @@
         if (!sharesViewport) return NO;
 
         if (!retiredClients) retiredClients = [[NSMutableArray alloc] init];
+        WineContentView *latest = retiredClients.lastObject;
         [retiredClients addObject:view];
         view.clientRetired = YES;
         view.clientBackingReady = NO;
-        [self addSubview:view positioned:NSWindowBelow relativeTo:nil];
+
+        /* Keep the latest fallback above earlier canvases and below live views. */
+        if (latest)
+            [self addSubview:view positioned:NSWindowAbove relativeTo:latest];
+        else
+            [self addSubview:view positioned:NSWindowBelow relativeTo:nil];
 
         /* Most handoffs finish at the next present or opaque GDI update.
          * Bound retention if the application hides the view without replacing it. */
